<section class="section reveal" id="matrix-properties">
  <span class="section-label">Advanced Topics</span>
  <h2>Matrix Rank, Condition Number, and Numerical Stability</h2>

  <p>Understanding matrix properties helps diagnose and fix numerical issues in algorithms.</p>

  <h3>Rank and Effective Rank</h3>

  <p>Rank tells you the dimensionality of the matrix's column space—how many independent columns it has.</p>

  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="cm"># Matrix rank</span>
<span class="va">A_full_rank</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">array</span>([[<span class="nm">1</span>, <span class="nm">0</span>], [<span class="nm">0</span>, <span class="nm">1</span>]])      <span class="cm"># Rank 2</span>
<span class="va">A_low_rank</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">array</span>([[<span class="nm">1</span>, <span class="nm">2</span>], [<span class="nm">2</span>, <span class="nm">4</span>]])      <span class="cm"># Rank 1 (2nd row = 2 * 1st row)</span>

<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Rank full: {np.linalg.matrix_rank(A_full_rank)}"</span>)  <span class="cm"># 2</span>
<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Rank low: {np.linalg.matrix_rank(A_low_rank)}"</span>)    <span class="cm"># 1</span>

<span class="cm"># Effective rank from SVD: number of singular values > threshold</span>
<span class="va">s</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">linalg</span>.<span class="fn">svd</span>(<span class="va">A_low_rank</span>, <span class="va">compute_uv</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="kw">False</span>)
<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Singular values: {s}"</span>)  <span class="cm"># [4.472... 0. ] or close to zero</span></code></pre>

  <h3>Condition Number: Measuring Numerical Stability</h3>

  <p>Condition number measures sensitivity to perturbations. Large condition numbers indicate ill-posed problems.</p>

  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="cm"># Condition number (ratio of largest to smallest singular value)</span>
<span class="va">A_well_conditioned</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">eye</span>(<span class="nm">2</span>)
<span class="va">A_ill_conditioned</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">array</span>([[<span class="nm">1e10</span>, <span class="nm">1</span>], [<span class="nm">1</span>, <span class="nm">1e-10</span>]])

<span class="va">cond1</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">linalg</span>.<span class="fn">cond</span>(<span class="va">A_well_conditioned</span>)
<span class="va">cond2</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">linalg</span>.<span class="fn">cond</span>(<span class="va">A_ill_conditioned</span>)

<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Well-conditioned: {cond1:.2f}"</span>)      <span class="cm"># ~1.0 (good)</span>
<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Ill-conditioned: {cond2:.2e}"</span>)   <span class="cm"># Very large (bad)</span>

<span class="cm"># Rule of thumb: 10^16 / condition_number ≈ precision loss</span></code></pre>

  <div class="key-takeaway">
    <h4>✦ Key Takeaways</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Rank reveals linear dependencies in columns</li>
      <li>Low-rank matrices can be approximated with fewer dimensions</li>
      <li>Condition number measures numerical stability (prefer cond ≈ 1)</li>
      <li>Large condition numbers cause precision loss in computations</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

